{
  "id": "lolin-d32",
  "name": "LOLIN D32",
  "baseChip": "esp32",
  "pcb": "black",
  "notes": [
    "LOLIN (WEMOS) D32: 57 x 25.4 mm ESP32-WROOM-32 (4 MB flash) with a CH340C bridge, micro-USB, and LiPo support (PH-2 connector + TP4054 charger, ~500 mA). Auto-flash circuit onboard - no BOOT button needed.",
    "GPIO35 is not broken out: it reads the battery through a 100k/100k divider (battery voltage = ADC reading x 2). The USB pad is raw VBUS and BAT is the battery terminal - there is no regulated 5 V output.",
    "Two enable pads: RST resets the ESP32, but the pad silkscreened EN enables the 3.3 V regulator - pulling THAT low powers off the whole board."
  ],
